// Game: Postretro
// Format: Standard
// E18 runtime-spawner test set piece, and the scripts-first complement to
// closet-reveal. Same sealed room and closet nook, but here the map carries the
// bare minimum: the trigger and mover hold only the KVPs that have no scripting
// equivalent, and every reaction lives in spawner-test.ts. The plate fires
// spawnFromSpawner to materialize fresh AI enemies at runtime (the path the
// round-1 feet-to-center fix touched). Watch that spawned enemies stand on the
// floor, not sunk into it, and walk out through the doorway.
// Compile: cargo run -p postretro-level-compiler -- content/dev/maps/spawner-test.map -o content/dev/maps/spawner-test.prl
// Run: cargo run -p xtask -- run content/dev/maps/spawner-test.prl
// Sealed room, interior 288 x 256 x 128 units, wall thickness 16, with a
// recessed closet nook carved into the solid east block. The nook interior
// spans x 176 to 272, y 96 to 160, z 0 to 96, entered through a doorway at
// x 176 that the sliding door occludes. The nook and main room form a single
// enclosed interior joined by that internal doorway, so the world hull is
// sealed with no leak. Worldspawn brush order: floor, ceiling, west, east,
// south, north walls, east block south of nook, east block north of nook,
// closet back wall, closet lintel, and the billboard-scatter comparison wall.
// Every brush is an axis-aligned box wound normal-inward, so there are no
// degenerate duplicate-point faces.
// Scripts-first authoring: the trigger names no reaction and commands no mover,
// so prl-build prints a benign [inert trigger] note. That is a static-view
// false positive; the compiler cannot see the onTriggerEvent binding in
// spawner-test.ts that owns the plate enter edge.
// NOTE: keep map comments free of braces and quotes; the .map parser does not
// fully strip // comments and those characters break the parse.
// entity 0
{
"classname" "worldspawn"
"initialGravity" "-9.81"
"wad" ""
"data_script" "../scripts/spawner-test.ts"
"_tb_mod" "dev"
"_tb_def" "external:../../../sdk/TrenchBroom/postretro.fgd"
